error Failure { Failed; }

// `source.branch.v1` (card `IF-STATEMENT`). The archetypal shape the custody
// join exists for: a resource released on both arms of a branch. Releasing it
// on only one is the conditional leak, and refuses at `Q046`.
//
// The condition is decidable at check time, exactly as the `succeeds` and
// `passes` literal outcome controls beside it are, so the reference
// observation, the CFG observation and the compiled program's own output are
// single-valued and comparable. What is *not* decided away is the branch: both
// arms are validated, both are emitted as real basic blocks, and the emitted C
// computes `3 < 5` itself.
fn main() -> i32 {
    let a = qcore_acquire(1, true, Failure);
    if (3 < 5) {
        drop a;
    } else {
        drop a;
    }
    return 0;
}
